  "worked_solution": "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}\u20610 \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
